From 7c2ac37007694c663fdad9291a053318b0e3217c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:58:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Intelligent mode: advanced UX, CSS and JavaScript through a
 controlled UX action layer

The copilot can now change how a survey looks and behaves - scoped CSS,
states, responsive rules, animations, behaviours and, on request,
JavaScript - as structured, validated operations, previewed on the real
components and applied as one undoable AI change.

- schema: SurveyDefinition.ux { styles, animations, behaviors } with
  targets by stable id (question, option code, block, page, button,
  progress, navigation, component) - carried by preview, test, publish,
  export and duplicate; absent, the runtime renders exactly as before.
- engine ux.ts: one target grammar for actions and scripts; selectors
  scoped under [data-rs-ux="<survey id>"]; one CSS gate for every value;
  scoped CSS text (html/body/:root, @import, sibling escapes refused,
  keyframes namespaced); compiled stylesheet with reduced-motion guard and
  device-preview parity; script validation (rs api only, no loops, no
  page/network/storage); item validation; reviewUx (dead targets,
  conflicts, duplicate animations, theme overrides, phone traps, global
  branding CSS); diffUx; runtime triggers (fire / hold / release).
- engine uxActions.ts: create/update/remove style, animation, behaviour;
  attach_behavior_to_*; create_responsive_rule. surveyActions: uxOnly
  refuses structural actions; structureUnchanged proves only ux changed.
- renderer UxLayer: compiled CSS, answered marks, stagger, page
  transitions, declarative behaviours, scripts in a sandboxed frame
  (opaque origin, no-network CSP, gated and rate-limited rs commands,
  re-validated before running).
- runtime: the shell names survey, block and page; nav buttons carry
  data-rs-button; the layer mounts only when the survey has UX.
- studio: UX guide sent on UX turns; look-only detection; outline lists
  existing UX by id and each named question's layout and styling;
  Changes panel "Look and behaviour" (items in words, the structure
  proof, a live preview on the real renderer - after/before/phone - and
  the generated code); UX tab (items, UX review, removal); applied note.

Tests: engine ux.test.ts (8), studio copilot.test.ts (+2), both mutation
checked; browser scripts/ux-copilot-test.mjs (13). Docs:
docs/INTELLIGENT-UX.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
